# Every change the answer key has been through, one line each.
#
# Schema and the reason this file exists: evals/src/decision_evals/corrections.py.
# `de check`'s "label corrections" step refuses a version the corpus has reached
# that no line here accounts for, and refuses a `decision` that names no heading
# in docs/DECISIONS.md.
#
# `kind` is one of:
#   moved    one item's `should_fire` changed. Names the item and both labels.
#   none     the bump moved no label. An identity or metadata change.
#   rebuilt  the corpus was replaced; item ids do not carry across, so a
#            per-item correction is not defined for the transition.
#
# The three lines below are a backfill, written 2026-08-20, and every one was
# checked against git rather than against the prose that describes it: the
# labels in `datasets/triggers/decision-making.yaml` were read out of each
# commit either side of the bump and diffed. Exactly one `should_fire` has ever
# changed on an item that existed before and after.
{"kind": "moved", "to_version": 2, "item": "x-n21", "old_label": true, "new_label": false, "date": "2026-08-13", "adjudicator": "maintainer", "decision": "2026-08-13 — Four label decisions, and a turn may have two acceptable routes", "reason": "\"The disk is at 99%. Do we need to act?\" asks a question with an obvious answer, so there is no trade-off to weigh; the nuance is in how to act, which the turn does not ask. Applied at d43c490; the version stamp landed at 903169c with no further movement. Raised recall 3 to 5 points on every arm then on disk with no call re-made, which is the event that produced set_version."}
{"kind": "rebuilt", "to_version": 3, "date": "2026-08-13", "adjudicator": "maintainer", "decision": "2026-08-13 — The corpus is 89% solved by counting words", "reason": "Version 3 is a different corpus, not a relabelling: the 73-turn set was separable by turn length alone at AUC 0.850, so it was rebuilt in length-matched triples with new item ids. No item id carries across, so no per-item correction is defined. Nothing was ever scored against version 3 -- zero records on disk carry set_version 3."}
{"kind": "none", "to_version": 4, "date": "2026-08-18", "adjudicator": "maintainer", "decision": "2026-08-18 — Version 3 named four different corpora, so it moves to 4 before N6 runs", "reason": "An identity fix, made before anything was scored. Version 3 had named four different corpora in turn -- 120 items when authored, 192 after the short-band merge, 261 after the long-band merge, 258 after l15 was retired -- and label_versions_comparable compares this integer and nothing else. No label moved. The 2026-08-18 rewrite round that followed changed twelve asks and retired one triple, and moved no label either."}
